{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/701141-how-do-you-use-strix-in-your-games","id":701141,"title":"How Do You Use Strix in Your Games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-14T11:18:10-07:00","id":701141,"title":"How Do You Use Strix in Your Games?","content":"So, the Strix. On the surface they seem like an odd choice as the primary antagonists for OP to choose for the core. They're nigh indestructible, largely undetectable, and have the potential to be utterly relentless, but it seems to me that's pretty fitting with the core of the game. VtR seems to be almost exclusively about vampire-on-vampire conflict, so it seems like these guys are best used as a force of nature that overturns the politics of the city, largely unassailable plot devices that characters have to deal with the consequences of.<br /> <br /> But I'm sure other people drew different conclusions. How have you guys utilized the Strix in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T11:36:53-07:00","id":701175,"title":"","content":"They're actually fairly destructible, the trick is that your <i>characters </i>are not likely to know that setting them on fire when they possess a corpse is the way to stop them.<br /> <br /> Characters need to take advantage of their banes, but they also need to know that the Owls have them in the first place. That kind of knowledge (and the dramatic irony wherein the <i>characters </i>might not know it even if the players do) is a great source of drama when using the Strix.<br /> <br /> The other thing to keep in mind is that because of the corpse jumping, Strix usually aren't an enemy that you beat up to death. The short story <i>Lullay, Lullay </i>is a great one by Joshua Alan Doetsch from the <i>Strix Chronicles Anthology </i>is pretty much a perfect example of a Strix antagonizing a vampire, and how they eventually deal with the Strix.<br /> <br /> So in part, your idea about force of nature is right. At the same time, it's really important to not forget that Strix (well, some of them) aren't just animals hunting Kindred, they're cunning and often times very very personal. Involve your players with the Strix up close. Maybe, if it's a schemer, it takes a particular interest in one member of the coterie, and either helps him advance or tears him down. Maybe the Strix claims to know secrets that it can share with them. The key is to make what the Strix does matter to the players, and make them feel something very strongly. The Strix don't tend to to elicit strong reactions, whether it's fear, horror, revulsion, envy, anger, so on.<br /> <br /> As an example, my girlfriend is GMing a game for us right now, and a Strix has shown up and made a big show of scaring everybody at a Sanctified Mass. Of course, it singled out one of our coterie, the one of us without a sire, and talked to her as if she was its long lost childe... Infront of <i>everyone</i>. It's an awkward situation that's not making us any friends, and the Strix has been appearing in corpses to talk to that coterie-mate while the rest of us are none-the-wiser. It claims to know things and want to show her things. Given that she's already been a bit of an outcast anyway, will she go along with the Strix? Will she dupe the rest of us? What does the Strix want with her, exactly? We don't know. All very exciting stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-14-2015, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T12:56:01-07:00","id":701251,"title":"","content":"In the last Chronicle I ST'ed, there were a handful of Striges harassing the Coterie of neonates\u2014and one of them 'befriended' the players for its own ends, but was never really friendly per se; it just seemed to derive more amusement than its fellows from pushing their buttons up close and personal rather than destroying them while it pursued its own ends. It even 'rewarded' them for their aid in the same way that a housecat will bring you a dead dismembered rodent as a gift, even when their actions weren't necessarily intended to help it.<br /> <br /> The rest of the city had varying reactions to the Striges, but since they had mostly conceived of them as fairy tales for Kindred (and mostly the Striges had it in for the Coterie more than anything else), the rest of the All Night Society largely ignored them unless the Coterie or the Striges directly interfered with them, mostly because it seemed reasonable to play up the sense of isolation for new Kindred and the &quot;What's in it for me?&quot; mentality of most vampires. One notable example was an old (but oddly not excessively powerful) Nosferatu claiming to have been embraced in the final years of the Camarilla, who recognized a Strix for what it was, but not how to fight it\u2014and then promptly went into torpor in hiding after putting her affairs in order and finding a way to use one of the players, a Haunt herself, as her catspaw while she was 'away'.<br /> <br /> The rest of the city's political landscape was kind of a shambles by the end, too, with the various covenants gaining or losing influence (or both) in tangling with the Striges. The players were basically caught between being manipulated or harassed by antagonists in the All Night Society . . . and being manipulated or harassed by each Strix. (TV Tropes calls this &quot;Not So Different, You And I,&quot; I think.)<br /> <br /> I never really gave one hundred percent clear motives on what they wanted or why, but the Striges wove in and out of the rest of the story and were balanced with other antagonists and events (and sometimes, as the Joker would have it, just gave things a little <i>push</i>, intentionally or otherwise). They were more a plot device or a phenomenon than just a clear enemy the Coterie could entirely defeat. They did destroy or contain some of them, but at the behest of another Strix\u2014itself loosely based on the Hunter and Teacher archetypes in the Strix chapter\u2014and ultimately the Striges did just as much damage, or more, than the Coterie could do to them.<br /> <br /> As both you and Leetsepeak have said, 'force of nature' is a good way to put it. The Striges may have a lot in common in terms of their abilities, but no one Strix is the same as any other\u2014they're all hellish black snowflakes in that regard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 10-15-2015, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T13:01:03-07:00","id":701256,"title":"","content":"I made them a major threat in my first <b>Blood And Smoke</b> / Second Edition game, Actual Play transcripts <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?734837-Vampire-The-Requiem-2nd-Edition-Nobody-Wants-You\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, making them a potentially overwhelming threat as they started to mass and take over Kindred, forcing the characters to investigate ways to stop them and eventually ally themselves with a repugnant elder vampire to defeat them. The focus on investigation and experimentation gave the game a more <b>Hunter</b> than <b>Vampire</b> feel at times, but there were still plenty of ugly secrets to uncover, leaving Kindred society divided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T23:59:04-07:00","id":701772,"title":"","content":"I'm currently using the Strix in a Hunter (Null Mysteriis) game. The game is a sort of X-files-like tour of the world of darkness for some new players. So far, the PCs have encountered a single Strix that is basically the force of nature you describe above. I started the Strix business with the &quot;Body of Evidence&quot; SAS from the Collection of Horrors. Agent Chalmers, from the SAS, has already eviscerated a unit of Task Force: Valkyrie and is turning out to be a terrible force to scare the PCs with. Granted, this Strix has stats and I have no intention of making it invulnerable. It's just a matter of finding its weaknesses and striking at the right opportunity... or letting it tear through the kindred population, if the PCs let it. It's a bit like a time bomb in that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Improper use of inverted commas, Hoover!&quot; - Herr Starr","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8536-nutshell","name":"Nutshell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T10:11:14-07:00","id":703641,"title":"","content":"I brought in a sighting of the Strix in my Game on Rpol... not sure WHY the strix are there just &quot;Being mysterious and sinister&quot;<br /> to weird out the PC's<br /> <br /> am thinking about them embracing at least one char...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T11:15:40-07:00","id":703664,"title":"","content":"In the werewolf game I'm running there's a fetish with two strix in it from way back in Aztec times. It's activated by filling a concavity in the device with fresh blood, and the players just think it's using some variant of warding gift, as it activates a variant of the Labyrinth Shadow Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}